      "content": "thanks. the thing is, the diary mentions a \"guardian\" who was tasked with keeping certain bloodlines from being tracked by the state, even after the empire fell. it mentions a specific sigil—a modified laurel wreath with a broken spear. i actually saw that exact symbol on a ring worn by the man i saw today in the North End. he was wearing it very subtly, like he didn't want it noticed, but it was unmistakable. do you think there's any precedent for secret societies or \"hidden lineages\" from the Roman era that might have used specific symbols to identify themselves while living in plain sight through the centuries?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
